<title>USA: LCRA 430 MW Texas gas plant returns to service.</title>
<headline>LCRA 430 MW Texas gas plant returns to service.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lower Colorado River Authority (LCRA) confirmed Thursday its 430 megawatt (MW) natural gas-fired Ferguson power plant returned to service Wednesday, as expected.</p>
<p>&quot;It came back 0315 (1515 CDT) yesterday,&quot; said spokesman Bill McCann.</p>
<p>The Marble Falls, Tx., generating station was shut a week ago following a superheater tube rupture.</p>
<p>The Ferguson facility produces eight percent of LCRA's electricity output.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1622</p>
</text>
